# Cloudflare Pages SPA fallback. Single-page marketing site for now;
# any future /docs, /blog, etc. paths gracefully route to index.html
# until they get their own files.
#
# NOTE: explicit /privacy → /privacy.html rules were dropped. Cloudflare
# Pages strips `.html` extensions automatically AND serves `<path>.html`
# when the user requests `<path>` — both behaviors combined to form an
# infinite redirect loop when our `_redirects` rule fought them. The
# privacy.html file in this directory is now served at /privacy via
# Cloudflare's default behavior, no rule needed. The SPA catch-all
# below only fires for paths that don't have a matching file.
/*  /index.html  200
